class jadx.core.dex.visitors.typeinference.TypeInferenceVisitor {
private boolean deduceType(MethodNode mth, SSAVar var) {
		if (var.isTypeImmutable()) {
			return false;
		}
		ArgType type = var.getTypeInfo().getType();
		if (type.isTypeKnown()) {
			return false;
		}
		// try best type from bounds again
		if (setBestType(mth, var)) {
			return true;
		}
		// try all possible types (useful for primitives)
		if (tryPossibleTypes(mth, var, type)) {
			return true;
		}
		// for objects try super types
		if (tryWiderObjects(mth, var)) {
			return true;
		}
		return false;
}
}
```


### Response Format:

**If the method CANNOT return null at this specific call site:**
```xml
<response>
  <reason><![CDATA[EXPLAIN WHY THE INVOCATION ClspGraph clsp = mth.root().getClsp() RESULT CANNOT BE NULL.]]></reason>
  <value>NO</value>
</response>
```

**If the method CAN return null at this specific call site:**
```xml
<response>
  <reason><![CDATA[EXPLAIN WHY THE INVOCATION ClspGraph clsp = mth.root().getClsp() RESULT CAN BE NULL.]]></reason>
  <value>YES</value>
</response>
```

**If you need declarations of other methods to make a determination:**
```xml
<response>
  <reason><![CDATA[Explain why you need these method declarations to make a confident decision]]></reason>
  <success>false</success>
  <methods>
    <method>methodName</method>
  </methods>
</response>
```

### Important Notes:
- Be precise and specific in your reasoning
